{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when He brings you.</b> So that you not say: HaShem did not command to sanctify only those who went out of Egypt — therefore it comes and teaches you here that even in the land they shall sanctify them." "<b>To the land of the Canaanite.</b> Because the sons of Heth honored Abraham the old man, and when they heard that HaShem had given the land to our forefathers, he arose and vacated before them. HaShem said: You vacated before the sons of Heth — in your lifetime the land shall be called by your name, and I shall give you another, good land — and which is that? Africa." "<b>As He swore to you.</b> 'And I shall give it to you as a heritage — I am YHWH.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The logic of 'in your lifetime the land shall be called by your name' follows the Hebrew חייך as 'your life' read with ארץ from the preceding clause; the sentence is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:37.311940556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}